{{also|post-haste|post haste}}
==English==
{{was wotd|2006|June|22}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|post-haste}}, {{l|en|post haste}}

===Etymology===
From the former instruction on letters ‘haste, post, haste’, later reinterpreted as a compound of {{compound|en|post|haste}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌpəʊstˈheɪst/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌpoʊstˈheɪst/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-posthaste.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-posthaste.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[quickly]], as fast as someone travelling post; with great [[speed]]
#: {{ux|en|It is imperative that you finish your task '''posthaste'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1946|[[w:Paramahansa Yogananda|Paramahansa Yogananda]]|[[s:Autobiography of a Yogi|Autobiography of a Yogi]]|chapter=Chapter 17|text="Sasi cannot last through the night." These words from his physician, and the spectacle of my friend, now reduced almost to a skeleton, sent me '''posthaste''' to Serampore.}}

